{"from":"all-mechanical-bosses","to":"plantera","type":"required-gate","note":"Plantera is a Hardmode boss that can be fought in the Underground Jungle after all three mechanical bosses (The Twins, The Destroyer, and Skeletron Prime) have been defeated.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Plantera","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Plantera","rev":1031902,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"brain-of-cthulhu","to":"skeletron","type":"recommended-next","note":"By this point, you should have at least Demonite, Crimtane, Meteorite, or Jungle equipment, with a fair range of weapons and accessories. A tough fight with Skeletron will grant you access to the Dungeon.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Guide:Game_progression","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Guide:Game_progression","rev":1029434,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"celestial-pillars","to":"moon-lord","type":"required-gate","note":"Pillars drop Lunar Fragments when destroyed, and destroying all four of them results in the spawn of the Moon Lord.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Celestial_Pillars","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Celestial_Pillars","rev":1031403,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"eater-of-worlds","to":"brain-of-cthulhu","type":"alternative-route","note":"The Eater of Worlds is the Corruption counterpart to The Crimson's Brain of Cthulhu.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Eater_of_Worlds","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Eater_of_Worlds","rev":1030072,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"eater-of-worlds","to":"skeletron","type":"recommended-next","note":"By this point, you should have at least Demonite, Crimtane, Meteorite, or Jungle equipment, with a fair range of weapons and accessories. A tough fight with Skeletron will grant you access to the Dungeon.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Guide:Game_progression","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Guide:Game_progression","rev":1029434,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"eye-of-cthulhu","to":"eater-of-worlds","type":"recommended-next","note":"Due to how helpful Corruption gear is, this will probably be the second boss faced in worlds that have Corruption, rather than worlds with The Crimson.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Bosses","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Bosses","rev":1031655,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"golem","to":"duke-fishron","type":"optional","note":"Fighting Duke Fishron is not required for game progression, but his defeat rewards the player with powerful weapons and equipment.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Duke_Fishron","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Duke_Fishron","rev":1032197,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"golem","to":"empress-of-light","type":"optional","note":"The Empress of Light, an optional boss, can be fought after defeating Plantera, but it is recommended to fight her after beating the Golem.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Guide:Game_progression","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Guide:Game_progression","rev":1029434,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"golem","to":"lunatic-cultist","type":"required-gate","note":"The Lunatic Cultist is summoned after killing the Cultists that spawn at the Dungeon's entrance after Skeletron and Golem have been defeated.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Lunatic_Cultist","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Lunatic_Cultist","rev":1029876,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"golem","to":"martian-madness","type":"required-gate","note":"Defeating Golem is a prerequisite for unlocking the Lunar Events, the Martian Madness, and Tier 3 of the Old One's Army.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Golem","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Golem","rev":1032187,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"hardmode","to":"duke-fishron","type":"early-challenge-possible","note":"While he can be summoned as soon as Hardmode is initiated, his difficulty is on par with that of a post-Golem boss, making him a serious threat to unprepared players.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Duke_Fishron","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Duke_Fishron","rev":1032197,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"hardmode","to":"duke-fishron","type":"required-gate","note":"While he can therefore be summoned as soon as the player enters Hardmode, defeating him will generally require gear obtained later on.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Bosses","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Bosses","rev":1031655,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"hardmode","to":"pirate-invasion","type":"required-gate","note":"The Pirate Invasion is a Hardmode invasion event that causes pirate-themed enemies to spawn in place of regular enemy spawns.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Pirate_Invasion","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Pirate_Invasion","rev":1032965,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"hardmode","to":"queen-slime","type":"optional","note":"She is an optional boss fight and is a small gap to challenge before facing the mechanical bosses, warranting equipment upgrades and other items.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Bosses","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Bosses","rev":1031655,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"hardmode","to":"queen-slime","type":"required-gate","note":"She is available to battle at the start of Hardmode, and is summoned from Gelatin Crystals which can be found in the Underground Hallow.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Bosses","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Bosses","rev":1031655,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"hardmode","to":"skeletron-prime","type":"required-gate","note":"Enabling Hardmode in a world is necessary for game progression, as several new bosses leading up to the game's final boss only become available to fight in this world state.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Hardmode","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Hardmode","rev":1033440,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"hardmode","to":"solar-eclipse","type":"required-gate","note":"A Solar Eclipse is a Hardmode event that begins to occur rarely after at least one mechanical boss has been defeated.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Solar_Eclipse","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Solar_Eclipse","rev":1033882,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"hardmode","to":"the-destroyer","type":"required-gate","note":"Enabling Hardmode in a world is necessary for game progression, as several new bosses leading up to the game's final boss only become available to fight in this world state.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Hardmode","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Hardmode","rev":1033440,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"hardmode","to":"the-twins","type":"required-gate","note":"Enabling Hardmode in a world is necessary for game progression, as several new bosses leading up to the game's final boss only become available to fight in this world state.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Hardmode","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Hardmode","rev":1033440,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"lunatic-cultist","to":"celestial-pillars","type":"required-gate","note":"are four late-Hardmode, stationary bosses that appear during the Lunar Events after the Lunatic Cultist has been defeated.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Celestial_Pillars","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Celestial_Pillars","rev":1031403,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"plantera","to":"empress-of-light","type":"early-challenge-possible","note":"While she can be summoned as soon as Plantera is defeated, her difficulty is on par with that of a post-Golem boss, making her a serious threat to unprepared players.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Empress_of_Light","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Empress_of_Light","rev":1027282,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"plantera","to":"empress-of-light","type":"required-gate","note":"Prismatic Lacewings spawn in The Hallow on the Surface between dusk (7:30 PM) and midnight (12:00 AM) once Plantera has been defeated.","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Empress_of_Light","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Empress_of_Light","rev":1027282,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
{"from":"plantera","to":"frost-moon","type":"required-gate","note":"The Naughty Present, which summons the Frost Moon, requires materials only available in Hardmode worlds where the player has already defeated Plantera","sourceUrl":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Frost_Moon","_prov":{"gameVersion":"1.4.5.8","sources":[{"kind":"curated","url":"https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Frost_Moon","rev":1025991,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13","overlay":"progression"}],"verified":true,"unverifiedFields":[],"editorialFields":[]}},
